## Current Astrotask Data Architecture

### Fields That Would Be Encrypted (Text/Sensitive)

| Model | Field | Current Type |
|-------|-------|--------------|
| Task | title | string |
| Task | project | string |
| Task | tags | string[] |
| Project | name | string |
| User | name | string |
| User | actionbar | string[] |

### Fields That Stay Unencrypted (Aggregation)

| Model | Field | Reason |
|-------|-------|--------|
| Task | duration | Needed for time tracking metrics |
| Task | session_count | Needed for counts |
| Task | column_index, position | Layout metadata |
| Task | status, is_active | Boolean flags |
| Session | duration, start_time, end_time | Time-series aggregation |
| All | created_at, updated_at | Time-series data |
| All | id, user_id | Relationships |

**Key Insight:** Your metrics dashboard (total time tracked, session counts, time-series charts) would continue to work because they aggregate on **numeric fields**, not encrypted text.

