## Implementation Architecture

### Option A: Full Client-Side (Recommended for True ZKE)

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    BROWSER                          │
│  ┌─────────────┐     ┌────────────────────────┐    │
│  │  Password   │────▶│  Key Derivation (KDF)  │    │
│  └─────────────┘     └───────────┬────────────┘    │
│                                  ▼                  │
│                    ┌────────────────────────┐      │
│                    │  Master Key (memory)   │      │
│                    └───────────┬────────────┘      │
│                                ▼                    │
│  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │
│  │  Encrypt on save │ Decrypt on load         │    │
│  │  (Web Crypto API: AES-256-GCM)            │    │
│  └────────────────────────────────────────────┘    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                         │
                         ▼ (ciphertext only)
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    SERVER                           │
│  • Stores encrypted blobs                          │
│  • Cannot decrypt anything                         │
│  • Can still aggregate on numeric fields           │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Key Derivation Flow
```typescript
// Frontend: When user logs in
async function deriveEncryptionKey(password: string, salt: Uint8Array): Promise<CryptoKey> {
  const keyMaterial = await crypto.subtle.importKey(
    'raw',
    new TextEncoder().encode(password),
    'PBKDF2',
    false,
    ['deriveKey']
  );

  return crypto.subtle.deriveKey(
    {
      name: 'PBKDF2',
      salt: salt,
      iterations: 600000, // Industry standard
      hash: 'SHA-256'
    },
    keyMaterial,
    { name: 'AES-GCM', length: 256 },
    false,
    ['encrypt', 'decrypt']
  );
}
```

