## Critical Trade-offs

### What You Gain
- **True privacy**: Server cannot read user's task titles, projects, or tags
- **GDPR-friendly**: Encrypted data = reduced compliance burden
- **Trust**: Users know their data is protected even from you
- **Breach protection**: Database leak reveals nothing readable

### What You Lose

| Concern | Impact |
|---------|--------|
| **Password recovery impossible** | If user forgets password, their data is GONE forever. No "reset password" for encrypted data. |
| **No server-side search** | Can't search tasks by title on the server. Search must be 100% client-side. |
| **Password change = re-encrypt everything** | Changing password requires decrypting all data with old key, re-encrypting with new key. |
| **Performance hit** | ~200ms key derivation on login. Decrypt all tasks on page load. |
| **Complexity** | Significant engineering effort. Easy to make security mistakes. |
| **Metrics limitations** | TopUser metrics currently show names/emails - these would be encrypted. |

